WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.630 --> 00:00:08.310
Hi, welcome back to the lamrim.

00:00:08.430 --> 00:00:13.380
Love in the Time of the Virus,
or we could call it 

00:00:13.380 --> 00:00:15.030
Sending the Virus to the Middle of the Sun.

00:00:15.330 --> 00:00:17.160
I'm not sure which one I like better.

00:00:17.720 --> 00:00:25.720
You saw one of my favorite images 
in the world, which is a croissant in Paris.

00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:28.560
 
You know, wandering around Paris, 

00:00:29.189 --> 00:00:32.250
I like to stop by every boulangerie I see.

00:00:32.670 --> 00:00:35.310
There's one, every three or four doors,

00:00:35.310 --> 00:00:38.160
so it's kind of difficult for me to walk through Paris.

00:00:38.720 --> 00:00:45.640
I got the recipe for that croissant 
and I tried to make it at home,

00:00:45.800 --> 00:00:48.420
it's almost a half a kilo of butter.

00:00:49.050 --> 00:00:53.970
So, I decided I shouldn't eat
so many. Anyway, they're delicious.

00:00:54.510 --> 00:00:58.410
Why we're talking about that? We're
going to, I also don't remember,

00:00:58.410 --> 00:00:59.310
Let's see! We're going to talk about it.

00:00:59.910 --> 00:01:00.360
Okay.

00:01:00.630 --> 00:01:03.540
He starts with a question. 
Pabongka Rinpoche starts with a question:

00:01:04.160 --> 00:01:07.160
RANG RE LA THUGS DAM GYI 
MTHIL GANG YIN DRIS NA, 

00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:10.520
So, if someone comes up and says to us,

00:01:10.620 --> 00:01:15.560
"Do you remember that word from last episode? 
We said something in the palm of your hand,

00:01:16.070 --> 00:01:18.260
and this is your main practice,

00:01:18.260 --> 00:01:21.285
this is like the number one practice you're working on,

00:01:21.285 --> 00:01:23.714
it's the one that's at hand all the time?"

00:01:24.340 --> 00:01:28.760
And if somebody comes up to you and says, 
"Hey man, what are you focusing on nowadays?

00:01:29.300 --> 00:01:32.300
What's your number one buddhist practice?"

00:01:32.720 --> 00:01:37.620
And I don't know about you, but if you're like me,

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:40.820
I've got practices and practices and 
practices and practices,.

00:01:40.980 --> 00:01:48.000
And I'll never forget, I had a student from 
Burma many years ago. Maybe 25, 30 years ago.

00:01:48.090 --> 00:01:51.090
He learned one more meditation from me.

00:01:51.740 --> 00:01:55.369
I was having a class and he said
"I don't know if I'm going to show up."

00:01:55.369 --> 00:01:57.020
And I said, "Why?"

00:01:57.735 --> 00:02:00.435
And he says "I don't need one
more thing to feel guilty about 

00:02:00.700 --> 00:02:04.880
that I'm not doing that you taught me."

00:02:05.060 --> 00:02:10.980
And he says, "I'm going a little bit 
crazy feeling guilty about trying 
to do all the things you've taught me."

00:02:12.640 --> 00:02:18.580
THUGS DAM GYI MTHIL means,
 THUGS DAM GYI MTHIL means 
what are you going to focus on?

00:02:19.100 --> 00:02:25.820
So, I think it's important for all of us to find 
one thing that you're going to be focusing on.

00:02:25.820 --> 00:02:31.360
Obviously, in this lamrim retreat 
that we're doing right now,

00:02:31.360 --> 00:02:36.480
we're trying to focus on the
idea of this experience.

00:02:36.780 --> 00:02:46.300
And I don't think we've really gotten
yet the instructions for triggering that experience.

00:02:46.420 --> 00:02:51.880
But still, I think hearing
about it over and over again is planting

00:02:52.010 --> 00:02:54.260
seeds in our mind to have that experience.

00:02:54.350 --> 00:02:56.209
And if we have that experience,

00:02:56.840 --> 00:03:02.260
then I believe, if enough of us have
this experience together,

00:03:02.360 --> 00:03:06.900
 then I think the virus couldn't survive around us.

00:03:07.740 --> 00:03:10.710
So, I think that that's my idea
on how to work on the virus.

00:03:10.710 --> 00:03:14.430
And then, I was having
breakfast and I was thinking,

00:03:14.430 --> 00:03:16.230
come on, you know, get real.

00:03:16.950 --> 00:03:20.640
You have to study the news this morning.

00:03:21.179 --> 00:03:23.970
You have to see what the
economists says about the progress

00:03:23.970 --> 00:03:26.070
with the virus vaccination.

00:03:26.730 --> 00:03:30.480
You have to think about is American Airlines'

00:03:30.630 --> 00:03:32.609
idea about flying planes safe?

00:03:33.140 --> 00:03:35.360
And I caught myself thinking like that. 

00:03:37.920 --> 00:03:42.480
Then they had an article about in some 
country people heard, people were going,

00:03:42.720 --> 00:03:49.860
 started, they heard that drinking methyl alcohol, 
which is poison, was good to prevent the virus.

00:03:49.880 --> 00:03:55.200
And 400 people died drinking hard alcohol

00:03:55.320 --> 00:03:56.940
that you use for cleaning.

00:03:57.649 --> 00:04:02.839
And then, I remember I was
thinking, "Oh, those people are crazy.

00:04:02.840 --> 00:04:09.900
They're living in such a strange society 
where they would drink methyl alcohol and die 

00:04:10.980 --> 00:04:15.080
because they drink a poison, because 
they thought it would help with them virus somehow."

00:04:15.140 --> 00:04:19.740
And then I caught myself and I
thought, "Well, the vaccination is the same." 

00:04:19.940 --> 00:04:23.180
 
It's actually based on a wrong idea.

00:04:23.270 --> 00:04:23.960
You see what I mean?

00:04:24.020 --> 00:04:26.240
It's, it's the same thing.

00:04:26.240 --> 00:04:27.169
If it works,

00:04:27.885 --> 00:04:33.305
if they make one that works, it's not
because of something in the chemicals.

00:04:33.395 --> 00:04:33.784
Okay?

00:04:34.355 --> 00:04:39.485
It's because of some kind
of attitude that you and I have.

00:04:39.485 --> 00:04:51.100
If we can have this bodhichitta experience,
if we can make contact with a few billion beings directly,

00:04:51.200 --> 00:04:56.220
 
and if we can comfort them and say,
"Don't worry, I'll take care of you, one by one."

00:04:56.320 --> 00:04:59.840
 
Then, that's the real antidote for the virus.

00:05:00.040 --> 00:05:04.640
And the vaccination and the methyl alcohol,
I think they're just about the same.

00:05:04.780 --> 00:05:08.880
 
If it works, it's because of your love.

00:05:08.880 --> 00:05:12.580
 
It's not because of what's in the vaccination.

00:05:13.680 --> 00:05:17.600
And I look forward to the 
vaccination and I think it'll work. 

00:05:17.680 --> 00:05:21.480
But I think we have to have a lot of love for it to work.

00:05:21.620 --> 00:05:23.780
We have to think about other people at this time.

00:05:24.380 --> 00:05:27.890
Anyway, if someone asks you, 
"So, what's your main practice Geshe La?"

00:05:28.250 --> 00:05:32.150
'Cause you know, by the way, I
have people come up to me and say,

00:05:32.810 --> 00:05:36.260
"You know, you've taught us like
a hundred different meditations,

00:05:37.160 --> 00:05:39.440
and well, which one you want us to focus on?

00:05:39.440 --> 00:05:43.040
Which should we hold in our, as our main practice?"

00:05:43.040 --> 00:05:46.600
 
And then he says, "Somebody asks you this question,

00:05:46.620 --> 00:05:49.980
,RTA MGRIN YIN, PHYAG RDOR YIN,
 'JIGS BYED 'DRA 'DON GYIN

00:05:50.160 --> 00:05:58.120
means, "Oh, my main practice is tantra,  
Hayagriva." Which means Horse Throat Tantra.

00:05:58.120 --> 00:05:59.267
It's a special tantra.

00:05:59.267 --> 00:05:59.840
PHYAG RDOR

00:06:00.320 --> 00:06:05.240
which means Vajrapani, the
Buddha with the Vajra in his hand.

00:06:05.320 --> 00:06:10.660
And then'JIGS BYED, which is Bahirava, 
which means the Frightener or the Lord of Terror.

00:06:11.880 --> 00:06:13.480
And 'DRA 'DON. These are difficult.

00:06:13.700 --> 00:06:19.715
'DRA 'DON GYIN  is a difficult word. 
"DRA means, "Oh, something like those three." 

00:06:19.715 --> 00:06:22.865
Or you could say 
VAJRAYOGINI, or you could 
say Tara, or you could say Medicine Buddha.

00:06:22.865 --> 00:06:25.205
"I'm focusing on that."

00:06:25.865 --> 00:06:29.255
'DON means I'm reciting

00:06:30.080 --> 00:06:32.640
that SADHANA. 
That's my regular SADHANA.

00:06:32.740 --> 00:06:35.040
'DON means to recite every morning.

00:06:35.180 --> 00:06:36.180
What's the Sanskrit?

00:06:38.420 --> 00:06:40.720
SVAD VI YA, SVAD VI YA.

00:06:41.200 --> 00:06:45.260
And it's a famous mistranslation
that people do of the Yoga Sutra.

00:06:46.240 --> 00:06:50.140
It means to do your daily memorization and recitation.

00:06:50.140 --> 00:06:53.340
And all the translations say 
self study,  or something like that.

00:06:53.340 --> 00:06:55.520
Which has nothing to do with that.

00:06:55.600 --> 00:07:03.240
Anyway, 'DON means 
SVAD VI YA. It means to recite 
your SADHANA every morning from memory.

00:07:03.240 --> 00:07:07.040
GYIN is the present participle.

00:07:07.460 --> 00:07:09.000
"I'm doing that everyday."

00:07:09.705 --> 00:07:11.205
"That's what I'm doing everyday."

00:07:11.840 --> 00:07:15.820
YOD ZER MOD,. 
ZER MOD means we say stuff like that, but,

00:07:16.460 --> 00:07:22.946
PHAL CHE BA NI,. 
Most of us, if you figure out
what's our THUGS DAM GYI,

00:07:22.946 --> 00:07:24.675
THUGS DAM GYI MTHIL

00:07:24.680 --> 00:07:28.840
NYON MONGS DUG GSUM. For $50.

00:07:31.900 --> 00:07:33.660
 DUG GSUM?

00:07:35.960 --> 00:07:37.760
Yea, $50 and you've got to remind me,

00:07:37.760 --> 00:07:38.750
I'll forget.

00:07:39.920 --> 00:07:40.460
Yeah.

00:07:40.790 --> 00:07:44.810
Most of us are ... 
most of us, what's our main practice?

00:07:44.840 --> 00:07:49.760
It's thinking that things come 
this way and then getting irritated with things,

00:07:49.760 --> 00:07:51.380
or else wanting things

00:07:52.229 --> 00:07:52.979
the wrong way.

00:07:53.430 --> 00:07:57.000
And that's our main, that's our core practice.

00:07:57.030 --> 00:07:58.110
You want a core practice?

00:07:58.140 --> 00:07:59.220
That's our core practice.

00:08:00.200 --> 00:08:02.480
Those three animals in 
the middle of the wheel life, 

00:08:02.480 --> 00:08:04.080
right there in the core of the wheel of life.

00:08:04.660 --> 00:08:07.540
DUG GSUM THUGS DAM GYI MTHIL 
DU BYED PA MANG NGO,,

00:08:07.580 --> 00:08:10.520
means you see a lot of people
like that. That's what's their's is.

00:08:10.520 --> 00:08:15.590
And I got a picture here
of just a palm of the hand,

00:08:16.310 --> 00:08:18.780
so you could remember this expression.

00:08:18.780 --> 00:08:20.760
What's our main practice?

00:08:20.840 --> 00:08:22.200
What's the thing we're focusing on?

00:08:22.830 --> 00:08:26.730
And it's this thing in the palm of 
the hand, where this is your main practice.

00:08:26.730 --> 00:08:29.520
 This is the one you carry around with you all the time.

00:08:29.900 --> 00:08:32.360
And I like this picture, I don't know why.

00:08:32.400 --> 00:08:35.040
I think it's kind of artistic, I guess.

00:08:35.720 --> 00:08:36.220
Alright,

00:08:38.020 --> 00:08:41.960
JO BO CHEN POS KYANG SNGAR 
CHOS THAMS CAD LA MKHAS PAR GYUR KYANG

00:08:42.060 --> 00:08:44.840
Then Lord Atisha, he's talking about Lord Atisha,

00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:49.800
Dipkankara Sri Janana, and he says, "Wow!

00:08:49.845 --> 00:08:51.765
He was a master of everything."

00:08:51.765 --> 00:08:56.440
He had mastered countless scriptures, 

00:08:56.500 --> 00:08:58.080
and commentaries are unbelievable.

00:08:58.280 --> 00:09:01.160
In fact, I was trying to read one 
yesterday and I was like ... 

00:09:01.280 --> 00:09:06.260
I actually decided not to teach it to you guys 
in October because it's just too difficult.

00:09:06.944 --> 00:09:10.740
And, so, CHOS THAMS CAD LA MKHAS PAR GYUR.

00:09:10.740 --> 00:09:14.180
He was a master of everything, of all these...

00:09:14.560 --> 00:09:16.040
By the way, we are going to do his SADHANA,

00:09:16.040 --> 00:09:21.000
but we're not going to do a commentary on emptiness

00:09:21.000 --> 00:09:22.860
which is often printed with the SADHANA.

00:09:23.760 --> 00:09:27.520
I thought it would be nice to
do them together, but it's too far out.

00:09:27.940 --> 00:09:30.660
It would take a year to teach it.

00:09:30.820 --> 00:09:33.689
MKHAS PAR GYUR KYANG DES THUGS MA TSIM PAR,

00:09:33.689 --> 00:09:34.871
THUGS MA TSIM PAR

00:09:34.880 --> 00:09:39.620
means, but he wasn't satisfied with 
learning all these topics. And, TSIM PAR,

00:09:41.340 --> 00:09:46.540
 TSIM PAR SEMS RIN PO CHE 'DI'I PHYIR.

00:09:46.960 --> 00:09:51.980
 SEMS RIN PO CHE is a beautiful
expression, which means this jewel mind,

00:09:52.180 --> 00:09:54.180
this jewell state of mind.

00:09:54.180 --> 00:09:58.740
Meaning this experience, 
having this experience with other people.

00:09:58.740 --> 00:10:01.160
SEMS RIN PO CHE, this jewel state of mind.

00:10:01.170 --> 00:10:04.480
PHYIR, for the sake of getting it,

00:10:04.480 --> 00:10:08.440
'DI'I PHYIR RGYA MTSOR GRU GZINGS BCAS TE. 

00:10:08.440 --> 00:10:14.240
He took off across the ocean
to get the instructions on bodhichitta.

00:10:14.260 --> 00:10:19.829
So, there was a famous lama living in SUDVARNADIPA

00:10:20.310 --> 00:10:25.439
The Golden Isle, which is Indonesia, part of Indonesia.

00:10:25.439 --> 00:10:26.069
What's it called?

00:10:26.849 --> 00:10:27.930
Sumatra.

00:10:29.920 --> 00:10:33.460
Anyway, he went off, he said 
"I heard there's a great teacher,

00:10:33.460 --> 00:10:40.420
of bodhichtta living in the 
isles around Java and Sumatra."

00:10:40.819 --> 00:10:47.510
So, he took off on a boat, 1000 years ago.

00:10:47.960 --> 00:10:53.500
This guy, this lama, took off from north India 

00:10:53.500 --> 00:10:57.820
and went all the way to the
ocean and then went 13 months.

00:10:58.180 --> 00:11:01.240
ZLA BA BCU GSUM 
GYI RING DKA' BA SPYAD 

00:11:01.540 --> 00:11:06.520
Extremely difficult journey.
Extremely dangerous journey.

00:11:06.820 --> 00:11:09.940
We have in this next image,

00:11:10.680 --> 00:11:13.840
I kind of feel like
this image says it all.

00:11:14.420 --> 00:11:23.720
He's in this tiny boat on a very dangerous sea 
and it was extremely dangerous to sail in those days.

00:11:23.760 --> 00:11:26.500
And I don't think this
painting is an exaggeration.

00:11:26.670 --> 00:11:28.290
Why is red important?

00:11:31.905 --> 00:11:33.314
He always wore a red hat.

00:11:34.574 --> 00:11:36.104
Tsongkapa wore gold one.

00:11:36.584 --> 00:11:43.574
So, if you see a thanka and they have a
red pundit hat, that's Atisha.

00:11:43.574 --> 00:11:45.214
And if it's gold, well, that's Tsongkapa.

00:11:45.214 --> 00:11:48.944
So, I picked the red ship and this is not an exaggeration.

00:11:48.944 --> 00:11:53.745
This is probably what it 
felt like to travel those 13 months,

00:11:54.555 --> 00:11:56.865
to travel across the ocean

00:11:57.405 --> 00:11:59.235
to meet this lama.

00:11:59.505 --> 00:12:03.915
And he was so strict with his vows that
he refused to take his monks robs off.

00:12:04.220 --> 00:12:06.865
He did the whole trip in his monks robs.

00:12:06.865 --> 00:12:08.320
And when he got there,

00:12:09.560 --> 00:12:11.640
What happened that was so famous when he got there?

00:12:18.920 --> 00:12:25.660
Yeah, I don't think it was 
that much, but he refused to go to,

00:12:25.660 --> 00:12:30.000
by the way that teacher's name was also 
Dharmakirti, but it's a different Dharmakirti.

00:12:30.220 --> 00:12:33.280
And sometimes he's called Suvanadipa Guru.

00:12:33.500 --> 00:12:36.680
The Lama from the Golden Isle, Sumatra.

00:12:37.500 --> 00:12:40.290
But he refused to go directly to his classes.

00:12:40.380 --> 00:12:45.520
He checked him out first. 
He probably got to Indonesia 

00:12:45.520 --> 00:12:48.920
and got an internet connection 
and checked out this person 

00:12:48.920 --> 00:12:52.660
to see if there were any scandals 
or any problems with this person.

00:12:54.180 --> 00:12:56.250
And he did not go directly to the teacher.

00:12:56.250 --> 00:13:00.360
He studied the teacher first,
after the 13 months on the ocean.

00:13:01.320 --> 00:13:04.880
BLA MA GSER GLING PA LA 'DI'I GDAMS NGAG YONGS RDZOGS GSAN TE 

00:13:05.720 --> 00:13:07.995
And then Lord Atisha

00:13:07.995 --> 00:13:11.655
studied the complete instructions

00:13:12.200 --> 00:13:21.320
for having this experience of bodhicitta directly 
from Lama Serlingpa, Suvanadipa Guru.

00:13:21.320 --> 00:13:24.820
GSAN TE BYANG CHUB KYI 
SEMS LA THUGS DAM GYI MTHIL 

00:13:25.240 --> 00:13:30.620
And he made bodhicitta,his palm practice,

00:13:30.780 --> 00:13:33.580
at the center of his palm practice.

00:13:33.580 --> 00:13:39.200
DE STON PA'I BLA MA LA
BLA MA GZHAN LAS GUS ZHABS CHE BAR MDZAD,

00:13:39.660 --> 00:13:43.320
And he had many, many teachers in his life, Atisha. 

00:13:43.320 --> 00:13:47.100
But he respected this teacher above all.

00:13:47.180 --> 00:13:53.150
And he was more devoted to this teacher than

00:13:53.150 --> 00:13:54.920
any other of his many teachers.

00:13:55.490 --> 00:13:57.860
The one who gave him the instructions on bodhicitta.

00:13:57.860 --> 00:14:02.260
GZHAN LTA BA NI GSER GLING PA 
SEMS TZAM YIN PAS DMA' BA YIN NO,,

00:14:02.560 --> 00:14:04.580
This is a very interesting sentence.

00:14:05.390 --> 00:14:06.470
GZHAN means,

00:14:07.890 --> 00:14:14.400
if you looked at this teacher, 
SUVANADIPA GURU, from another point of view,

00:14:14.400 --> 00:14:22.710
GZHAN LTA BA, 
his  LTA BA, his philosophical 
school was SEMS TSAM.

00:14:24.570 --> 00:14:26.430
He was a mind only practitioner.

00:14:27.300 --> 00:14:29.130
Therefore he was DMA' BA .

00:14:30.510 --> 00:14:32.550
He was lower, lower school.

00:14:33.060 --> 00:14:36.030
And it's very interesting that
Pabongka Rinpoche would throw that in.

00:14:36.585 --> 00:14:41.595
From the point of view of his emptiness understanding, 

00:14:41.595 --> 00:14:43.725
he was actually lower than Atisha,

00:14:43.725 --> 00:14:45.800
and Tsongkapa and people like that.

00:14:45.800 --> 00:14:49.620
His viewpoint was middleway, sorry, mind only.

00:14:51.280 --> 00:14:55.640
So, why should Atisha, whose viewpoint is much higher,

00:14:56.325 --> 00:14:59.535
respect this teacher above all his teachers?

00:15:00.015 --> 00:15:03.165
It's because he taught him this form of love.

00:15:03.195 --> 00:15:03.855
Universal love.

00:15:04.600 --> 00:15:05.980
That's very beautiful.

00:15:07.160 --> 00:15:11.900
DE'I PHYIR RANG RES 
BYANG CHUB KYI SEMS 'DI NYID 
RGYUD LA BSKYED AE THUB BLTA DGOS TE,.

00:15:11.900 --> 00:15:13.600
Say AE THUB. AE THUB.

00:15:13.920 --> 00:15:15.300
AE THUB, means,

00:15:15.600 --> 00:15:17.440
"Yeah, I got to do it."

00:15:18.300 --> 00:15:21.140
AE THUB. AE THUB, means,

00:15:21.620 --> 00:15:23.120
RANG RES means us guys,

00:15:24.060 --> 00:15:25.980
we should work on this.

00:15:26.010 --> 00:15:27.510
This is the practice we should work on.

00:15:27.840 --> 00:15:30.240
AE TUB means, "I think I can do it."

00:15:31.260 --> 00:15:32.320
AE THUB.

00:15:32.760 --> 00:15:35.060
THUB means to be able to, right?

00:15:35.060 --> 00:15:36.020
 AE THUB means

00:15:36.599 --> 00:15:40.199
"Yeah, I think I could do it. After hearing this lam rim,

00:15:40.685 --> 00:15:46.655
due to the hard work of Tim and Jigme
and Seiji and a hundred other people."

00:15:47.380 --> 00:15:50.340
You should be saying by now, in this course, 

00:15:50.560 --> 00:15:54.100
 AE THUB, "Hey, I think I can pull that off.

00:15:54.115 --> 00:15:56.785
I think I could do that. I want to go for it."

00:15:57.835 --> 00:15:58.314
 AE THUB.

00:15:58.920 --> 00:15:59.520
BLTA DGOS TE.

00:15:59.520 --> 00:16:00.860
That's how you have to think.

00:16:01.155 --> 00:16:02.155
